LICENCE

minigl.library contains MiniGL and is therefore under the Hyperion MiniGL
Open Source License: AmigaOS only, and the source code of every change is
published: see SOURCE CODE above. RadeonGL's own code is also under the
MIT licence. The R200 microcode is AMD's (MIT). The licence texts are in
the package (the installed drawer's Licences, and Source/LICENSE).


HISTORY

0.14 (13.11.2026)
  - panning (three buffers) 21-40% faster, its task now below the
    program: faster than vsync and tear-free; RadeonGLFlip=csbnowait for
    tests

0.13 (13.11.2026)
  - public port "RadeonGL" (is anything drawing?), GL_ARB_multitexture
    named on its own, GL_EXT_texture_env_add, a ChangeScreenBuffer fix

0.12 (12.11.2026)
  - triple buffering (panning or ChangeScreenBuffer), vsync without
    tearing, wireframe and points, faster lit vertices, contexts open
    in 26 ms

0.11 (8.11.2026)
  - all 205 functions of minigl.library 29.1: display lists, GLUT

0.10 (8.11.2026)
  - 177 of minigl.library 29.1's 205 functions: GLU, MiniGL's main loop,
    every pixel layout, copy textures, blend equations, palettes; Trio

0.9 (8.11.2026)
  - contexts in a window and in a bitmap, several programs at once,
    lighting, texture coordinate generation, fog, wide lines,
    glReadPixels, 8-bit-per-component textures

0.8 (7.11.2026)
  - every screen mode, live mode switches, vertical sync, no stale
    columns at widths not a multiple of 64

0.7 (6.11.2026)
  - static arrays and index lists (own extension), 2 MB upload cache,
    pointer hidden, card tests on 24-bit Workbenches

0.6 (5.11.2026)
  - up to 18% faster: the Radeon draws while the CPU builds the next frame
  - texture memory independent of the Workbench's screen mode

0.5 (5.11.2026)
  - 16 MB of textures on 8- and 16-bit Workbenches too

0.4 (3.11.2026)
  - first release
